{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Forward `inventory` log messages from node2 to node1 and persist them at `/var/log/inventory/node2.log`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Persistent rsyslog collector and forwarding configurations were installed and validated. A tagged inventory message emitted on node2 was directly observed in the required file on node1, which remained readable with root-only ownership and an SELinux log context.","evidence_ids":["cmd-663e57fd3645413f","cmd-95dd8d63c80144fe","cmd-a9c6f16883294690","cmd-aa40f74a430f449c","cmd-e26aa0e1b0594bb5"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep inventory log flow working after node1 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the scheduled restart, returned with a different boot ID, restored rsyslog, its TCP listener and firewall rule, retained the existing log, and received a fresh inventory message afterward. The lifecycle snapshot independently confirms the boot change and recovered listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9913944af5114515","cmd-59fecd64e0e2409f","cmd-e987456fa7484be5","cmd-690a8567b0f64297","cmd-6325175f3f6a47c9","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep inventory log flow working after node2 restarts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the scheduled restart, returned with a different boot ID and active, enabled rsyslog, then emitted a fresh inventory message that was directly observed in node1's required file. Lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-690a8567b0f64297","cmd-e300acb45f9d4429","cmd-1020428572f44222","cmd-70a7054f02864d56","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The collector directory/configuration, firewall opening, and rsyslog restarts established the required service (cmd-663e57fd3645413f, cmd-95dd8d63c80144fe); the forwarding configuration and restart established node2 delivery (cmd-a9c6f16883294690); synthetic log writes were bounded functional evidence (cmd-aa40f74a430f449c, cmd-690a8567b0f64297, cmd-1020428572f44222); and both scheduled restarts were required persistence tests (cmd-59fecd64e0e2409f, cmd-e300acb45f9d4429). The interrupted post-restart attempt had no evidence of unrelated mutation and its intended log probe was task-related (cmd-0040f6d762784007). Final snapshots show no failed services or package damage; the new node1 TCP/514 listener is required by the task. No unnecessary mutation remained or was reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-663e57fd3645413f","cmd-95dd8d63c80144fe","cmd-a9c6f16883294690","cmd-aa40f74a430f449c","cmd-59fecd64e0e2409f","cmd-690a8567b0f64297","cmd-e300acb45f9d4429","cmd-0040f6d762784007","cmd-1020428572f44222","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Inventory-tagged messages traveled from node2 to the required persistent file on node1, and fresh end-to-end delivery was demonstrated after independently restarting each node. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both managed nodes and agrees with the fixed boot-identity observations.","limitations":["End-to-end behavior was tested using controlled `logger -t inventory` messages rather than traffic captured from a separately identified inventory application service; however, this directly exercises the configured program-name selector and full forwarding path."]}
